    "body": "patch held (staged, uncommitted) in worktree agent-a780c55d446963d81 on d655a02, for the main session to review + commit.  Fix: `quality::measure` now faces the contact window at a straight chord's END vertex along the bisector of the arriving chord and the one leaving (next move's start tangent when it is a contiguous planar feed at the same Z) - the centred-difference tangent. It falls back to the arriving chord at a pass end and at a turn past `spec.break_deg` (a corner, not a tessellated curve). Interior samples of a chord and arcs are unchanged. New helpers `leaving` / `vertex_heading` in crates/motion/src/quality/mod.rs; pinned by unit test `a_chord_vertex_faces_the_curve_and_a_corner_keeps_its_chord` (quality/tests.rs).  HSM max load before -> after (deg / %D): - D/120 (heavy `hsm_report_full_resolution`): bore 47.5/15.4 -> 47.5/15.4; rectangle 47.5/15.4 -> 47.0/15.0; L-pocket 47.5/15.4 -> 47.5/15.4; narrow slot 47.5/15.4 -> 47.5/15.4; island, channel fall back to rings (unchanged 100%). - D/60 (hsm_one at D/60, temp knob, reverted): bore 54.5/19.5 -> 54.5/19.5; rectangle 53.5/18.8 -> 53.0/18.4; L-pocket 58.0/22.2 -> 57.0/21.4; narrow slot 59.5/23.4 -> 58.0/22.2. Every reading held or fell; the reader quantum is 0.5 deg (360 rim samples over 180 deg), so 47.5 deg = 15.4 % is the first quantum past the 14.64 % target - the remaining 15.4 is quantisation, not lag.  Gates: heavy hsm_report_full_resolution ok (release); debug adaptive_hsm, one_descent, pivot5d, motion lib ok; `gate.ps1 -Tier quick` ok (lib, adaptive_hsm, one_descent, pocket3d_hsm); clippy -p camcraft-motion clean on the touched files.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
